# TypeScript Rules

## Strict Mode — Always On

Every `tsconfig.json` in every folder must have:
```json
{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "strict": true,
    "noUncheckedIndexedAccess": true,
    "noImplicitReturns": true,
    "noFallthroughCasesInSwitch": true
  }
}
```

Never disable strict mode. Never add `@ts-ignore`. Use `@ts-expect-error` with a comment only when absolutely unavoidable.

## Type Annotations

```typescript
// ✅ Always type function parameters and return values
function calculateFocusScore(sessions: ModeSession[]): number { }

// ✅ Always type async function returns
async function getUserMetrics(userId: string): Promise<UserMetrics> { }

// ❌ Never use `any`
function process(data: any): any { }

// ✅ Use `unknown` when type is uncertain, then narrow it
function process(data: unknown): string {
  if (typeof data === 'string') return data
  throw new Error('Expected string')
}
```

## Naming Conventions

```
PascalCase     → types, interfaces, classes, React components, enums
camelCase      → variables, functions, methods, object keys
SCREAMING_CASE → constants, enum values
kebab-case     → file names (mode.service.ts, user.repository.ts)
```

## File Naming

```
mode.service.ts         → service files
mode.repository.ts      → repository files
mode.controller.ts      → controller files
mode.model.ts           → mongoose model files
mode.types.ts           → type definition files
mode.routes.ts          → route files
useMetrics.ts           → React hooks (camelCase with use prefix)
MetricCard.tsx          → React components (PascalCase)
```

## Interfaces vs Types

```typescript
// ✅ Use interface for object shapes that may be extended
interface UserMetrics {
  userId: string
  modeTime: ModeTimeEntry[]
}

// ✅ Use type for unions, intersections, primitives, utility types
type ChartType = 'line' | 'bar' | 'pie' | 'radar' | 'area'
type PartialMetrics = Partial<UserMetrics>
```

## Null Safety

```typescript
// ✅ Always handle null/undefined explicitly
const user = await UserRepository.findById(id)
if (!user) throw new NotFoundError('User not found')

// ❌ Never assume a query result is non-null
const user = await UserRepository.findById(id)
return user.email  // crash if user is null
```

## Async / Await

```typescript
// ✅ Always use async/await — never .then().catch() chains
const result = await someService.doThing()

// ✅ Always wrap async route handlers — errors propagate to error middleware
router.get('/metrics', asyncHandler(async (req, res) => {
  const data = await MetricsService.getUserMetrics(req.user.id)
  res.json(data)
}))

// ❌ Never leave floating promises
someAsyncFunction()  // unhandled rejection risk

// ✅ Explicitly void or await
void someFireAndForgetFunction()
await someImportantFunction()
```

## Enums

```typescript
// ✅ Use string enums for readability and debuggability
enum ModeType {
  DEV       = 'dev',
  CHILL     = 'chill',
  DEEP_WORK = 'deep_work',
  STUDY     = 'study',
  CUSTOM    = 'custom',
}

// ❌ Avoid numeric enums — values are meaningless in logs
enum Status { ACTIVE, INACTIVE }  // 0, 1 — confusing
```

## Imports

```typescript
// ✅ Group imports: external → internal → types
import express from 'express'
import { z } from 'zod'

import { ModeService } from '../services/mode.service'
import { asyncHandler } from '../utils/async-handler'

import type { Request, Response } from 'express'
import type { ModeSession } from '../types/shared/mode.types'
```

## No Magic Numbers or Strings

```typescript
// ❌ Magic numbers
if (sessions.length > 50) { }
const ttl = 900

// ✅ Named constants
const MAX_SESSIONS_PER_PAGE = 50
const JWT_ACCESS_TTL_SECONDS = 900
if (sessions.length > MAX_SESSIONS_PER_PAGE) { }
```
